/**
 * The `mask` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
 * [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
 * property hides an element (partially or fully) by masking or clipping a specified area of the
 * image. It is a shorthand for all the
 * [`mask-*`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask#constituent_properties)
 * properties. The property accepts one or more comma-separated values, where each value corresponds
 * to a
 * [`<mask-layer>`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask#mask-layer).
 *
 * Initial: mask-image: none; mask-mode: match-source; mask-repeat: repeat; mask-position: 0% 0%;
 * mask-clip: border-box; mask-origin: border-box; mask-size: auto; mask-composite: add. Inherited:
 * no.
 * Percentages: mask-position: refer to size of mask painting area minus size of mask layer image
 * (see the text for `background-position`).
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - add: The associated mask image is placed over all mask layers below it (with the corresponding
 * compositing operators applied). This is the default value. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-composite
 * - alpha: Indicates that the alpha (transparency) values of the mask image should be used. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-mode
 * - border-box: The painted content is clipped to the border box. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-clip
 * - content-box: The painted content is clipped to the content box. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-clip
 * - exclude: The non-overlapping regions of the associated mask image and the mask layers below it,
 * with their corresponding compositing operators applied, are combined. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-composite
 * - fill-box: The painted content is clipped to the object bounding box. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-clip
 * - intersect: The parts of the associated mask image that overlap all composited mask layers below
 * it replace those previously composited layers. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-composite
 * - luminance: Indicates that the [luminance
 * (brightness)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask#understanding_luminance)
 * values of the mask image should be used. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-mode
 * - match-source: Indicates that the type of mask is determined by the source. This is the default
 * property value. - If the `mask-image` references an SVG `mask`, its `mask-type` property value is
 * used, or its `mask-type` attribute, if present. If neither is explicitly set, this value defaults
 * to `luminance`. - If the mask image source is an `image` or a `gradient`, the `alpha` values of
 * the mask image are used. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-mode
 * - no-clip: The painted content is not clipped. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-clip
 * - no-repeat: The mask image is not repeated (and hence the mask painting area will not
 * necessarily be entirely covered). The position of the non-repeated mask image is defined by the
 * `mask-position` CSS property. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-repeat
 * - none: This keyword is interpreted as a transparent black image layer. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-image
 * - padding-box: The painted content is clipped to the padding box. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-clip
 * - repeat: The image is repeated as much as needed to cover the whole mask painting area. Mask
 * images along the edges are clipped when the size of the [mask origin
 * box](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-origin) is not an
 * exact multiple of the mask image's size. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-repeat
 * - repeat-x: The equivalent of `repeat no-repeat`. The image is repeated in the horizontal
 * direction as many times as needed to cover the width of the mask painting area. Mask images along
 * the right or left edges, or both depending on the `mask-position` value, will be clipped if the
 * width of the mask origin box is not an exact multiple of the mask image's width. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-repeat
 * - repeat-y: The equivalent of `no-repeat repeat`. The image is repeated in the vertical direction
 * as many times as needed to cover the height of the mask painting area. Mask images along the top
 * or bottom edges, or both depending on the `mask-position` value, will be clipped if the height of
 * the mask origin box is not an exact multiple of the mask image's height. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-repeat
 * - round: The mask image is repeated as many times as possible in its original dimensions. If the
 * size of the mask origin box is not an exact multiple of the mask image's size, all mask images
 * will be rescaled, [shrinking or
 * stretching](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask#rounded_repetitions)
 * to ensure no repetitions are clipped. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-repeat
 * - space: The mask image is repeated as many times as possible without clipping. If the element's
 * origin size is at least twice the size as the mask image's size in the associated dimension, the
 * `mask-position` property is ignored and the first and last images are positioned at the edges of
 * the mask origin container. If the mask origin box is not an exact multiple of the mask image's
 * size, whitespace is distributed evenly between the repeated mask images. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-repeat
 * - stroke-box: The painted content is clipped to the stroke bounding box. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-clip
 * - subtract: The associated mask image is placed, where it falls outside of all mask layers below
 * it (with the corresponding compositing operators applied). See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-composite
 * - view-box: Uses the nearest SVG viewport as reference box. If a
 * [`viewBox`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Reference/Attribute/viewBox)
 * attribute is specified for the element creating the SVG viewport, the reference box is positioned
 * at the origin of the coordinate system established by the `viewBox` attribute and the dimension
 * of the reference box is set to the width and height values of the `viewBox` attribute. See
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-clip
 *
 * Grammar: <mask-layer>#
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-masking-1/#propdef-mask
 *
 * Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask
 *
 * Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
 *
 * Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
 *
 * Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.
 */
